    "speaker_source": "heuristic",
    "speaker_source_detail": "Heuristic (text-based speaker guess)",
    "start": 1689.1599999999999,
    "end": 1721.2399999999998,
    "text": "I live in that neighborhood, and I personally, along with all a lot of my friends that grew up in that neighborhood group playing in there. And that's kind of where I got the basis for what I want to do in the world. Why I want to be an environmental studies major? Why I want to go into repairing our ecosystems because how our kids supposed to learn to care about something if it's not there. You know, we don't need a bike path. We have as other people have mentioned renewing infrastructure within the next five years. We have already existing trail plans that need to be attended to."
